hello everyone i'm dr umar malik and  welcome to math simplified  vitamin d also known as the sunshine  vitamin is a big topic right now  it comes as a surprise for most people  because they have never really had a  problem before and most of us believe  that a low vitamin d level change is  nothing  and it will not be a problem for us  anytime soon  well now vitamin d deficiency and  insufficiency is a global public health  problem  a conservative estimate tells us that  more than 1.3 billion people worldwide  are deficient for vitamin d  so in this video we will talk about how  vitamin d deficiency is a serious issue  and why you must take active steps to  treat vitamin d deficiency  vitamins are considered as essential  nutrients because either your body  cannot make them or they are made in  inadequate amounts they prevent negative  health consequences or diseases and are  vital for the optimum functioning of our  body  but vitamin d is special unlike other  vitamins it can be made by our body when  exposed to sun hence the name sunshine  vitamin  an estimated 80 of our total vitamin d  in our body comes from sun exposure to a  skin terms like crickets and  osteomalacia are commonly thrown around  when you talk about vitamin d deficiency  but research and years of clinical  experience has shown that the health  consequences of vitamin d deficiency not  only affects the bones but has far  reaching consequences for the whole body  researchers have found an alarming  number of health issues outside of its  role with bone diseases these include  certain cancers obesity and  cardiovascular diseases autoimmune  diseases  certain infections including covet 19  inflammatory bowel diseases and mental  health issues including various  psychological and cognitive disorders  so keeping that in mind let's start from  the very beginning  let's look at what are the common causes  of vitamin d deficiency the reasons vary  from insignificant causes like  inadequate exposure to sunlight and more  serious conditions like kidney and liver  problems  number one dark skin color melanin is  what gives skin its color  light skin people have less melanin than  those with darker skin  melanin is important because more  melanin means darker skin and darker  skin means natural sun protection  however as less sunlight can cross the  skin  dark skinned individuals require at  least three to five times longer  exposures to make the same amount of  vitamin d as a person with a white skin  tone research has also proven that  african american population has a mean  vitamin d level less than that of white  americans  number two is limited exposure to the  sun this is by far one of the most  common reasons of vitamin d deficiency  today as industrialization progressed we  tend to spend more time indoors most  adults work indoors and wear more  clothing during the work week which  leaves only minimal of the body exposed  to sunlight for short periods so they  cannot meet their vitamin d needs  through the sun alone  even if you do have some exposure to the  sun the total amount of vitamin d you  can produce is affected by many factors  like the season time of the day ozone  amount latitude and the number of clouds  in the sky  additionally increased awareness of skin  cancers has led to an incremental rise  in the use of sun protective creams  which are known to decrease the vitamin  d synthesis process  number three is being overweight or  obese  being overweight or obese may put you at  a risk for vitamin d deficiency a recent  review of 23 studies has shown that  obese people had 35 higher rates of  vitamin d deficiency compared with the  normal weighted subjects  while diet and decreased sun exposure  may have some impact on this there  appears to be an increased need that  cannot be met without a supplement  number four mal absorption and unhealthy  diet  people who have nutritionally  underwhelming and insufficient diets are  at a higher risk of developing vitamin d  deficiency  also people with a history of previous  gut surgeries unhealthy gut and  malabsorption syndromes for example  crohn's or celiac disease are often  unable to absorb enough vitamin d from  their diet which leads to a deficiency  number five is certain medications and  medical conditions  a wide variety of medications including  antifungal medications anticonvulsants  steroids and medications to treat aids  in hiv can enhance the breakdown of  vitamin d and lead to its low levels  also conditions like liver failure and  kidney failure interfere with the body's  natural pathways of synthesizing vitamin  d  if you are interested in learning more  about how our body synthesizes vitamin d  and how vitamin d acts in our body we'll  be uploading a video sometime soon so  make sure to subscribe to our channel  and hit the bell icon  well now that we know why vitamin d  deficiency occurs we can now ask the  question what are the health risks of  vitamin d deficiency  looking back in the mid 1600s two  gentlemen by the name of whistler and  glsen reported that children living in  industrialized cities in great britain  had short stature and had deformities of  the skeleton especially of the lower  legs a disease well known today as  ricketts which occurs due to the vitamin  d deficiency in children  however it wasn't until 1889 that  physicians discovered that sunbathing  was important for preventing rights  since then many other health benefits of  vitamin d and risks associated with  deficiency have been reported let's take  a look at a few of these  number one are skeletal diseases now  this is a common knowledge that vitamin  d is important for your bones but how  exactly that happens is as follows  vitamin d enhances the absorption of  calcium and phosphorus in your diet and  without it only 10 to 15 percent of  calcium and phosphorus are absorbed from  your diet thus vitamin d maintains the  optimum blood calcium levels to enable  your bones to remain healthy and strong  vitamin d deficiency leads to bone loss  osteopenia osteomalacia osteoporosis and  eventually increased risk of fractures  also there are vitamin d receptors in  human muscles that have a direct effect  on muscle strength this is evident from  the fact that severe vitamin d  deficiency can cause myopathy or  abnormal muscle function which can cause  muscle weakness and pain  treating vitamin d deficiency in elderly  population has been shown to decrease  knee and hip pain  a study of 769 older adults aged 50 and  80 years found that moderate vitamin d  deficiency positively predicts the  incidence of worsening of knee pain and  possibly hip pain over the next two to  five years  number two autoimmune diseases  autoimmune diseases are those disorders  in which the body's defense mechanism  misfires and starts acting out against  the body's own cells  now where exactly does vitamin d fit in  the case of autoimmune diseases is  unclear but there has been research that  shows a definitive link between vitamin  d deficiency and developing autoimmune  disorders  now take for example the case of type 1  diabetes in finland  type 1 diabetes is also an autoimmune  disorder the recommended daily dosage of  vitamin d was gradually reduced from  4000 units per day in 1964 in finland to  400 units per day in 1992. during this  period the incidence of type 1 diabetes  increased by more than 350 percent in  children aged between one to four years  even more convincing data came in 2006  when finland authorities made it  mandatory for all dietary milk to be  fortified with vitamin d2 and following  which the incidence of type 1 diabetes  platitude and begin to decrease  similarly current evidence supports that  vitamin d deficiency increases the risk  of developing multiple sclerosis which  is another autoimmune disease and  vitamin d supplementation alters the  disease activity in people with multiple  sclerosis  also a review of studies shows that in  people with multiple sclerosis having  adequate levels of vitamin d were  associated with fewer lapses  also they had lower risk of development  of new lesions in the brain had lesser  disability and lesser disease severity  and better long-term memory  number three cancer  cancer is a dreadful disease and  unfortunately we are still struggling to  fight it effectively years after years  of research have tried to isolate the  various risk factors that potentially  cause cancers in humans  one such risk factor being studied is  vitamin d deficiency a number of studies  have investigated whether people with  higher vitamin d intakes or higher blood  levels of vitamin d have lower risks of  specific cancers the results of these  studies however have been inconsistent  but these studies have suggested that  there may be an association between  increased risk of various cancers for  example colon cancer breast cancer  ovarian cancer skin cancer and prostate  cancer among people who are living far  from the equator  since these people get fewer sunlight  exposure to the skin they have an  increased prevalence of vitamin d  deficiency  number four cardiovascular diseases also  known as heart diseases  the term cardiovascular not only refers  to the heart but also to the conductive  vessels that help the heart push blood  to the whole body namely the arteries  veins and capillaries  a review of six studies that included  over 6400 people found that patients  with cardiovascular disease who  additionally had lower levels of vitamin  d  had more severe and advanced diseases  compared to those who had optimum levels  of vitamin d  vitamin d deficiency is associated with  an increased risk of hypertension that  is high blood pressure  also hyperlipidemia also known as high  cholesterol peripheral vascular diseases  coronary heart rate diseases myocardial  infarction or heart attack heart failure  and stroke the anti-inflammatory effects  of vitamin d may be the reason for this  and studies are ongoing to examine this  relationship  number five increased prevalence of  infections  it's possible that maintaining adequate  vitamin d levels could lessen the length  and severity of upper respiratory tract  infections and possibly even prevent  them  this was proven by a review of 12  studies including  2279 children  the study found that children with lower  respiratory infections had significantly  lower vitamin d levels compared with  normal healthy children  also there was a relationship between  how low the vitamin d level went and how  severe the infection was  this is especially important in the  current scenario of koved a latest study  in israel had surprising results the  researchers found that being deficient  in vitamin d before contracting covid19  had a direct impact on how severe the  disease will be and eventually how  lethal it became  the study revealed that 26 of the people  who had a pre-infection deficiency or  vitamin d diet compared to only three  percent of those who had higher levels  of vitamin d a staggering difference of  23 percent  while the researchers do not point to  vitamin d deficiency as being the cause  of death it states that if vitamin d  levels were low the disease was severe  and there was increased mortality in an  independent manner  whether or not vitamin d supplementation  helps in covet 19 is still understudy  however the author of the study says  that it is vital that people maintain a  healthy level of vitamin d in their body  as it may help them fight against  scovid19 infection  well friends with this we come to the  end of this video stay tuned for more  such content and leave a like or a  comment if you'd like to know more about  vitamin d  you can also consider becoming a member  on our youtube channel or support us via  patreon  do comment in the comment section below  for some topics for you like to make us  a video about  we at mad simplified are committed to  bringing you the latest content  till then take care stay safe and do  treat yourself to some good sunshine  every now and then
 

